<title>USA: TABLE-Johnson &amp; Johnson Q2 net income up.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Johnson &amp; Johnson Q2 net income up.</headline>
<dateline>NEW BRUNSWICK, N.J. 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Q2						  1997	1996</p>
<p> Sales to customers			 $  5,698  $  5,382</p>
<p> Cost of products sold			 1,749     1,732</p>
<p> Net earnings					909  $    791</p>
<p> Net EPS					     .68  $    .60</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding		1,332.5   1,332.9</p>
<p>  SIX MONTHS					1997	1996</p>
<p> Sales to customers			 $ 11,413  $ 10,716</p>
<p> Cost of products sold			 3,521     3,451</p>
<p> Net earnings				    1,818     1,581</p>
<p> Net earnings per share			 1.36	1.19</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding		1,332.9   1,332.8</p>
<p>	     (In Millions Except Per Share Figures)</p>
<p>NOTE: The impact of the stronger dollar relative to foreign currencies decreased second quarter sales by 3.2 percent, the company said.</p>
<p>For the six-month period, the strength of the U.S. dollar relative to foreign currencies created a negative impact of 3.1 percent during this period.</p>
</text>
